Place a file named .env in this folder which contains the following:

DATABASE_HOST=<db host name>
DATABASE_USER=<db user name>
DATABASE_PASSWORD=<db password>
DATABASE_DB=<db user name>

Make sure the username and password match the settings in database.yml

The content will be used to set the variables when creating the containers.

In VSCode or Antigravity reopne the folder in a devcontainer using Shift-CMD-P on a Mac.
Previously, docker needs to be installed an the docker daemon must be running. 
On MacOS use the Docker Desktop installer to get the daemon. Install docker-compose
using brew install docker-compose.

When opened in a devcontainer, run bundle install and then rails db:create && rails db:migrate. When the seed files are in place, run rails db:seed.

Then do a rails assets:precompile.

Then run rails server